WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.375
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
It's officially

00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:03.360
week two of Google
Cloud Next OnAir, which

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.510
means we're focusing on
productivity and collaboration.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.940
I'm Mark Mirchandani, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.390
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.150
Week two is all about
productivity and collaboration,

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.925
meaning we want
to help you work.

00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:18.300
So we've got a
lineup of sessions

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.940
that should appeal to
everyone, including end user

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.570
tips with easier collaboration
with G Suite, advice and guides

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.240
for IT admins managing
employee resources with Chrome

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.180
Enterprise, and key
insights for decision-makers

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.030
with questions around
security and availability.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.670
Be sure to add the talks you're
interested in to your playlist,

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.760
where you can watch
them on demand.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.720
With the challenges of
COVID-19, things are different.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.730
At Google, our focus
is on how to adapt

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.890
both internal and
externally, which

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.198
is why we use the same
products that we offer.

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:51.240
That's why I'm excited
about the solution keynote

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.220
this week with Javier
Soltero, the vice

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.770
president and general
manager for G Suite.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.750
He'll share some context
on how G Suite aims

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.860
to enable employees to have
impact wherever they are.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.540
Javier is also joined by
Hilda Clune, the technology

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.270
and transformation leader
of PricewaterhouseCoopers,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.700
so that you can hear directly
from a company relying on G

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.880
Suite to empower their people.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.920
One session on my own
playlist is G Suite

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.020
for Developers, where
Charles Maxson will

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.580
give an overview
of the many ways

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.290
to build tools with G Suite.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.790
There's a full
spectrum of options,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.120
from low-code tools that enable
users to build customizations

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.740
to the APIs and
professional tools

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.960
that empower software
vendors to build integrations

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.220
with G Suite.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.647
Add it to your own
playlist to check it out.

00:01:32.647 --> 00:01:34.980
Finally, as we move further
into this virtual conference

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.710
experience and discuss
the virtual tools to get

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.390
our work done, it
seems only right

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.983
that we highlight a demo
with a virtual pro tip.

00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:43.650
It's hard to feel
connected to your team

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.270
when your office
is closed, which

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.520
makes a remote-friendly
all-hands a useful tool

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.290
for keeping that team spirit.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.670
This video demo
shows you how you

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.400
can use Google Meet to host
a fully online all-hands

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.770
with up to 100,000 viewers.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.810
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:58.820
check out the link.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.280
Do you have any
thoughts or ideas?

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.080
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.550
We'll see you in the cloud.

